From df8fbafae081321f3c9a9c774e41007200913f32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:29:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] Wire the Windows node's chain consumers to the explicit
 local verifier

ENCLAVE_CHAIN_AUTHORITY=verifier + ENCLAVE_CHAIN_VERIFIER (loopback; validated when
windows/node/chain.mjs loads, so a bad value stops the node) now governs the Windows node's
actual readers, through the shared LeaseReader shipped in its admission bundle
(network/verified-read-client.mjs, exported by network/host-admission-node.mjs):

- chain.mjs splits the generic client by capability. State reads (book, registry, ledger,
  catalog, balances, earnings, proof-of-time) are proof-backed verified reads; the paged
  ledger enumeration and the catalog version/schema/config-CID read each run at ONE verified
  block; checkpoints anchor to the verified block and plan at it. Nonce, simulation,
  estimates, fees, broadcast, receipts, logs and transaction input go only to an explicit
  ENCLAVE_CHAIN_TX_RPCS transport, else refuse by name. BASE_RPCS and its public defaults
  are never used in this mode; rpcUrls() is empty.
- chain-reader.mjs is the one agreed() reader factory for owner-committed Shield startup
  (host.mjs), the ownership CLI (host-onchain.mjs) and check-endpoint (host-identity.mjs):
  the legacy quorumReader by default, the verifier-mode LeaseReader when chosen, with no
  public client constructed.
- session-api-auth.mjs gains an optional coherent snapshot mode (factory, session and owner
  facts at one verified block, uncached); the agent uses it under the verifier. Default
  reads and caches are unchanged.
- host-onchain.mjs reads balances from the verified state client and sends only through the
  explicit transport; the agent's sponsored registration uses the transaction client.
- network-enroll.mjs writes the network agent's chain section with the verifier instead of
  the RPC list (a switch either way restarts the agent once); node-config.example.cmd
  documents the settings for node-config.local.cmd.
- windows/node/host-admission.bundle.mjs rebuilt from this tree (candidate build, sha256
  28778491ccd6f56bd7a5a823408692e9229b73ae6a91835bbbe26549e234611a).

The legacy default is unchanged. Tests: real modules in child processes with counting
loopback stand-ins, the shipped deploy-files closure staged and loaded, and a canonical reth +
Helios E2E (state reads, admin book migration, ownership, session termination, tampered or
missing witnesses and a stale head).
